<title>BRAZIL: No cold in sight for Brazil coffee regions - Somar.</title>
<headline>No cold in sight for Brazil coffee regions - Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee regions face no risk of damaging cold in the next five to seven days, with polar air masses all passing to the south of the country, local meteorologists Somar said on Monday.</p>
<p>Minimum temperatures in the last 24 hours ranged between eight degrees Celsius in Pocos de Caldas, traditionally Brazil's coldest coffee region, to 14 degrees Celsius, Somar said.</p>
<p>Sunshine and clear skies should hold throughout the region until July 16 when a cold front should bring cloudier weather and scattered showers to Parana state and the south and west of Sao Paulo, it added.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
